{"name":"Moccasin","hex":"#fbebd6","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"moccasin","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A traditional Native North American shoe, usually without a heel or sole, made of a piece of deerskin or other soft leather turned up at the edges which are either stitched together at the top of the shoe, or sewn to a vamp (a piece covering the top of the foot). .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A modern shoe with either a low or no heel resembling a traditional Native American moccasin in that the leather forming the sides of the shoe is stitched at the top."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/moccasin"}],"entries":[{"title":"Moccasin","blocks":[{"text":"A moccasin is a shoe, made of deerskin or other soft leather, consisting of a sole and sides made of one piece of leather, stitched together at the top, and sometimes with a vamp. The sole is soft and flexible and the upper part often is adorned with embroidery or beading. Though sometimes worn inside, it is chiefly intended for outdoor use."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Airwalk_Men%27s_Mason_Mocassin_Slippers.JPG/330px-Airwalk_Men%27s_Mason_Mocassin_Slippers.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moccasin","wikidata":"Q252484"},{"title":"Moccasin (horse)","blocks":[{"text":"Moccasin was an American Thoroughbred Champion racehorse. In a career that lasted from 1965 to 1967, she ran twenty-one times and won eleven races. She remains the only two-year-old filly to be voted United States Horse of the Year. Moccasin won only one race in each of her two subsequent seasons but was an effective performer over sprint distances."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Moccasin_Grave.jpg/330px-Moccasin_Grave.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moccasin_(horse)","wikidata":"Q6887496"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Osage_%28Native_American%29._Pair_of_Moccasins%2C_early_20th_century.jpg/250px-Osage_%28Native_American%29._Pair_of_Moccasins%2C_early_20th_century.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Osage_%28Native_American%29._Pair_of_Moccasins%2C_early_20th_century.jpg/330px-Osage_%28Native_American%29._Pair_of_Moccasins%2C_early_20th_century.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Osage_%28Native_American%29._Pair_of_Moccasins%2C_early_20th_century.jpg/250px-Osage_%28Native_American%29._Pair_of_Moccasins%2C_early_20th_century.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOsage_(Native_American)._Pair_of_Moccasins%2C_early_20th_century.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Soft_moccasin.jpg/250px-Soft_moccasin.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Soft_moccasin.jpg/500px-Soft_moccasin.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Soft_moccasin.jpg/250px-Soft_moccasin.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASoft_moccasin.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Hopi_Pueblo_%28Native_American%29._Dancing_Shoes%2C_late_19th_century.jpg/120px-Hopi_Pueblo_%28Native_American%29._Dancing_Shoes%2C_late_19th_century.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b